# UI components

> Purpose: every screen is assembled from this catalog. Page and element transitions: `transitions.mdc`. Build each component once in `components/ui/<group>/`, show it on the **component page**, then reuse it. Tokens and principles: `ui-styling.mdc`. Form chrome: `forms.mdc`. States and icons: `icons-states.mdc`.

## Rules

### 1. Component Spec (the signature for every component)
```
### <Name> — <purpose in one line>
- Anatomy:     <parts / slots: e.g. header · body · footer · leading icon · action>
- Variants:    <visual/size/tone variants — from tokens only>
- States:      default · hover · focus-visible · active · disabled · loading · error · empty (only those that apply)
- Props/API:   <name: type = default — keep small; a11y props required where noted>
- Layout:      Mobile <…> · Tablet <…> · Desktop <…>   (Layout Responsive) — or reflow note (Normal)
- A11y:        <role · keyboard · label · focus behavior>
- Tokens:      <color · radius · shadow · spacing it uses>
- Customize:   className (root) · classNames slots (<anatomy keys>) · pass-through attrs — see §1b
```
The catalog below is the *minimum* each component must cover; the full spec goes in the component's file header or on the component page.

### 1b. Customization contract — follow the catalog; adjust per usage with `className`
The catalog component is always the starting point. When **one specific piece of content** needs a different look, the AI adds classes to that usage instead of forking or hand-building a lookalike.

1. **Follow first:** use the catalog component and its variants/props. Never re-create a component that exists.
2. **API every component exposes:** `className` (applied to the root, merged **last** so it wins) · `classNames` for multi-part components (keys = the anatomy names in its spec, e.g. `{ root, header, body, footer, icon, label }`) · `...rest` (native attributes, `data-*`, `aria-*`) · `ref`. Merge with `cn()` = `twMerge(clsx(base, variant, className))`, so precedence is **base < variant < className**.
3. **Choose the right scope:**
   | Change is needed… | Do this |
   |-------------------|---------|
   | in **one usage** | `className` / `classNames` at that usage |
   | in **3+ usages** | promote to a variant/prop (cva) in the component; update its spec and component-page entry |
   | **everywhere** / brand-wide | change the theme token |
4. **Allowed in an override:** spacing · sizing (keep touch targets ≥ 44px) · layout/position/alignment · responsive variants (`md:` `lg:`) · typography from the scale · colors from tokens (`bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`) · radius/shadow tokens · visibility per class · motion tokens · grid/flex.
   **Not allowed:** raw hex or arbitrary color values · `!important` / `!` prefix · inline `style` for color/spacing · removing focus ring/outline · shrinking below touch target · hiding required labels · changing semantic roles · z-index outside the scale.
5. **Specify it where the content is defined** (spec first, `format.mdc`): each override is recorded in the route block's `Overrides:` line (`route-layouts.mdc`) or the unit's Function Spec (`implementation-phases.mdc`) as `Component → classes → why`. The code carries exactly those classes. An override with no spec line is not allowed.
6. **The AI may add or change `className` itself** whenever the content calls for it, and updates the `Overrides:` line in the same change. Later-added classes replace earlier ones for that usage only; other usages are unaffected.
7. **Native flavor:** `cn()` lives in `lib/cn.js` (tailwind-merge or an ordered class-join); components accept a `className` string (and `classNames` object) the same way.

```jsx
// R-07 OrdersMobile.jsx — a denser summary card on mobile only
<Card className="p-3 md:p-5 bg-card/60" classNames={{ header: 'pb-2', footer: 'justify-between' }}>
```
```
Overrides: Card (order summary) → p-3 md:p-5 bg-card/60; header: pb-2; footer: justify-between → denser on mobile, roomy from tablet up
```

### 2. Organization
```
components/ui/{foundations,layout,nav,actions,overlays,inputs,lists,media,app,network}/   ← groups A–K (network only if the concept has it)
components/states/   NotFound, ErrorState, EmptyState
lib/hooks/           useViewClass, useDisclosure, useToast, useForm, … (reference/components/hooks.md)
```
Each file exports one component + its types; variants are props, never copies.

### 3. Component page (required, dev builds only)
Route `/_components` (excluded from production builds and SEO): every component × variant × state, in light **and** dark, at mobile · tablet · desktop widths. It is the visual contract — a component is `done` when it appears here.

### 4. Universal requirements
- Tailwind utilities + theme tokens only; no raw hex, no inline styles for spacing/color
- Touch target ≥ 44px; `focus-visible` ring on every interactive element; hover never the only affordance
- Keyboard: Tab order logical; Esc closes overlays; arrows for menus/tabs/lists/calendars; Enter/Space activate
- Loading → skeleton/loader; empty → `EmptyState`; error → inline message + retry
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; dark mode via tokens
- `aria-label` for icon-only; live regions for alerts/toasts/progress; correct `role`s (below)
- Lazy-load heavy components (`Chart`, `Player`, `Camera`, `Slides`, pickers, `NetworkTree`)

